-// sibling byte through git at a PER-RUN HEAD SNAPSHOT (one `rev-parse HEAD` per
-// lane at meter start, then `git cat-file -p <head>:<path>` for every byte
-// read — the working tree is never read). The snapshot heads are printed in the
-// output receipt, and every delta lane row must bind exactly those heads (a
-// sibling that moved between ledger regeneration and the meter run is
-// `lane-screen-head-mismatch`). Runtime-vocabulary notes carried from v18:
