-//      status must equal the status the meter re-derives from the sibling's
-//      bytes at its snapshot head (sibling-absent, unchanged, moved with a note
-//      naming a verbatim line, stale, file-absent).
-//   P2 roster completeness: every sibling lane dir at --fleet (git repos other
-//      than tabi-shokunin) is covered by the ruled map OR the delta ledger.
-//   P3 bounded delta screen: one `lane` row binds the screened bytes
-//      (provinceSha256, lines, bgHits, head — all at the snapshot head) and
-//      every BG hit line carries a `line` row whose quote is a verbatim whole
-//      line with a disposition in the frozen vocabulary. The r51 host-shape fix
-//      (symlinked lane entries, dot-entries skipped) and the r56 raw-byte sha
-//      discipline are unchanged.
-//
-// Round 59 delta (C1's FROZEN declared change set (a)-(e)); verify() differs
-// from v18 only by these hunks:
-//   (a) generation relabel: AUDIT_REL/DELTA_REL point at
-//       corpus/adjacency-host-{audit,delta}-r59.tsv, every schema string is
-//       tabi-adjacency-host-v19 (die, selftest, run output), the predicate
-//       sentence names the r59 ledgers and the new (d)/(e) clauses, and the
-//       usage lines and this header name round 59.
-//   (b) ROUTED r58-closure D5/N1: the harness truth table gains the
-//       findings-mismatch rows — a mismatched finding expectation returns false
-//       even when the predicate term matches and even when the count term
-//       matches. Two new selftest cases assert those rows against caseOk, the
-//       ONE verdict function the run loop uses, so a findings-term drop in the
-//       harness can no longer survive.
